/private/var/folders/80/jm5p82hn56g0crpvv9xjzrc00000gn/T/jc2-lane.9FRnN1/inputs/keller-pencil-genus-review-grok46-20260902.md:137:`z_u = L ∩ L_∞`, generic on `L_∞`. The 0-cycle `Φ^*(z_u)` is supported on components `C` with `Φ(C)=L_∞`: contracted components of `T_+` map to finitely many points of `L_∞`, avoided by genericity; dicriticals map onto `A_F`-bar, which meets `L_∞` in a finite set (the places at infinity of `A_F`), likewise avoided. `H2` is **not** required for that last sentence — only that `A_F`-bar `∩ L_∞` is finite. For generic `z_u`, `Φ|_C: C → L_∞` is unramified of degree `k_C`, and distinct such `C` do not share points over `z_u`. So `# Φ^{-1}(z_u) = Σ k_C = κ` geometric points.
