/private/var/folders/80/jm5p82hn56g0crpvv9xjzrc00000gn/T/jc2-lane.9FRnN1/inputs/keller-pencil-genus-review-grok46-20260902.md:209:- **Jacobian.** `Jac F_{m,k} = m x y^{m-1}` (chain rule, `Jac ψ_k=1`). Not a unit for `m≥1`. Non-Keller.
/private/var/folders/80/jm5p82hn56g0crpvv9xjzrc00000gn/T/jc2-lane.9FRnN1/inputs/keller-pencil-genus-review-grok46-20260902.md:210:- **Geometric degree.** On `{Q=V}`, `x=U−V^k` and `(U−V^k) y^m = V`. Generic `(U,V)=(3,5)`: squarefree of degree `m` in `y` (discriminant nonzero at the three charged pairs). `N=m`, independent of `k`.
/private/var/folders/80/jm5p82hn56g0crpvv9xjzrc00000gn/T/jc2-lane.9FRnN1/inputs/keller-pencil-genus-review-grok46-20260902.md:212:- **Genus, independent RH.** Cyclic `m`-cover `y^m = −w/(w^k +(β/α)w − t/α)`: ramification `(m−1) + k(m−1) + (m−gcd(k−1,m))`, so `2g−2 = (m−1)k − 1 − gcd(k−1,m) = (m−1)(k+1) − m − gcd(k−1,m)`. `θ_inf=gcd(k−1,m)=κ` (§3.3). Affine ramification at `w=0` is `m−1`. The pairing identity of §2.4 then gives `Z·R_aff = m−1 = N−1`, **constant in `k`**.
/private/var/folders/80/jm5p82hn56g0crpvv9xjzrc00000gn/T/jc2-lane.9FRnN1/inputs/keller-pencil-genus-review-grok46-20260902.md:217:(m,k)   N  n  κ=gcd(k-1,m)  2g−2 closed  g closed  g (3,5,7)  g (2,11,3)  Jac
/private/var/folders/80/jm5p82hn56g0crpvv9xjzrc00000gn/T/jc2-lane.9FRnN1/inputs/keller-pencil-genus-review-grok46-20260902.md:223:The producer grid `m=1,2,3` × `k=2..6` was rerun (15/15; `m=1` gives `g=0`). Family (A) sample `2g−2=N−1−gcd(c,N)−gcd(c−1,N)`: `(N,c)=(2,1) g=0; (3,2) g=1; (8,2) g=3; (8,5) g=2; (5,2) g=2` (5/5). For `m≥2`, `g→∞` at fixed `N=m`. `Z·K_X=(m−1)(k+1)−2m−gcd(k−1,m)→+∞`, matching `NVM:637-639` as data.
/private/var/folders/80/jm5p82hn56g0crpvv9xjzrc00000gn/T/jc2-lane.9FRnN1/inputs/keller-pencil-genus-review-grok46-20260902.md:227:### 5.2 THEOREM PROFILE-WITNESS, including Jac
/private/var/folders/80/jm5p82hn56g0crpvv9xjzrc00000gn/T/jc2-lane.9FRnN1/inputs/keller-pencil-genus-review-grok46-20260902.md:229:`G_k = ψ_k ∘ (x, x y^4 − y^2)`. `H = (x, Q)` with `Q = x y^4 − y^2`; `Jac G_k = Jac H = 2y(2x y^2−1)` for every `k` (chain rule). **Not a unit.** Non-Keller, as claimed.
/private/var/folders/80/jm5p82hn56g0crpvv9xjzrc00000gn/T/jc2-lane.9FRnN1/inputs/keller-pencil-genus-review-grok46-20260902.md:231:**`N=4`.** Substitution `x=U−V^k`, `(U−V^k) y^4 − y^2 − V = 0`. At generic `(U,V) ∈ {(3,5),(7,11),(−2,3)}` this is squarefree of degree 4 in `y` (discriminant nonzero) for `k=1,2,3`. Geometric degree 4.
/private/var/folders/80/jm5p82hn56g0crpvv9xjzrc00000gn/T/jc2-lane.9FRnN1/inputs/keller-pencil-genus-review-grok46-20260902.md:233:**Cycle type `1^2 · 2`.** On `H`: `s Y^2 − Y − w = 0` with `Y=y^2`. As `s→0`, `Y_− → −w` (two finite `y` if `w≠0`) and `Y_+ ∼ 1/s`, `y ∼ ± s^{−1/2}` (one 2-cycle). So `a=2`, `μ=2`, `S=1`, `W=2`, `N=a+W=4`. Left automorphism `ψ_k` does not change source cycle type. `[P3]`: `a+W=N`. `(C1)`: `2a=4≥4`. `7.B'`: `μ=2≥2`.
/private/var/folders/80/jm5p82hn56g0crpvv9xjzrc00000gn/T/jc2-lane.9FRnN1/inputs/keller-pencil-genus-review-grok46-20260902.md:235:**`(K)`.** Lemma 4.1: `N − a_P = r_P W + K_P`. Generic point of `A_F`: `a_P=2`, `r_P=1`, `K_P=0`. Origin (`V=0`, `U=0`): the specialised equation is `−y^2=0`, one affine point `(0,0)`, so `a_P=1`; with `r_P=1` (smooth curve, next paragraph) `K_P = 4−1−2 = 1 = a−1`. Sum of covering defects is `a−1`. If `(K)` were summed only over *singular points of the curve* `A_F`, the sum would be `0 ≠ 1`. Producer `KPG:491-496` already scopes this: the match is numerical/combinatorial, and `A_F` is smooth, which MI Prop 6.1 forbids under Keller. Confirmed with that scope.
/private/var/folders/80/jm5p82hn56g0crpvv9xjzrc00000gn/T/jc2-lane.9FRnN1/inputs/keller-pencil-genus-review-grok46-20260902.md:237:**`A_F`.** Escape for `H`: `y=t`, `x=t^{−2}+w t^{−4}` gives limit `(0,w)`, so `A_H={U=0}`; then `A_{G_k}={U=V^k}`. Gradient `(1, −k V^{k−1})` never vanishes. Smooth, irreducible, rational, one place at infinity, `n=k`. `H2` *shape*, not Keller.
/private/var/folders/80/jm5p82hn56g0crpvv9xjzrc00000gn/T/jc2-lane.9FRnN1/inputs/keller-pencil-genus-review-grok46-20260902.md:242:k   deg(3P+5Q−7)  g (3,5,7)  g (2,11,3)  2g_D−1   N  a  W  S  μ  Jac
/private/var/folders/80/jm5p82hn56g0crpvv9xjzrc00000gn/T/jc2-lane.9FRnN1/inputs/keller-pencil-genus-review-grok46-20260902.md:248:Matches `KPG:489`. No listed numerical profile datum bounds `g_L` in the dominant class. The Keller-derived requirement that `A_F` be singular is not a profile datum; it is `OPEN[SING-WITNESS]`.
/private/var/folders/80/jm5p82hn56g0crpvv9xjzrc00000gn/T/jc2-lane.9FRnN1/inputs/keller-pencil-genus-review-grok46-20260902.md:252:## 6. Item (f) — `NOETHER-K` alone, and what “alone” means
/private/var/folders/80/jm5p82hn56g0crpvv9xjzrc00000gn/T/jc2-lane.9FRnN1/inputs/keller-pencil-genus-review-grok46-20260902.md:254:**Verdict: CONFIRMED as a theorem about one identity.** **GAP** if promoted as “the only remaining Keller input is the polar tree”.
/private/var/folders/80/jm5p82hn56g0crpvv9xjzrc00000gn/T/jc2-lane.9FRnN1/inputs/keller-pencil-genus-review-grok46-20260902.md:256:NVM’s scope note (`NVM:640-642`, replayed at `KPG:524-527`): the families that send `Z·K_X → +∞` at fixed `N` “work” because of the affine ramification term `Z·R_aff`, which Keller kills. That diagnosis is quantitatively false in NVM’s own family (B).
/private/var/folders/80/jm5p82hn56g0crpvv9xjzrc00000gn/T/jc2-lane.9FRnN1/inputs/keller-pencil-genus-review-grok46-20260902.md:258:General ramification pairing (`NR:220`, `KPG:299-302`):
/private/var/folders/80/jm5p82hn56g0crpvv9xjzrc00000gn/T/jc2-lane.9FRnN1/inputs/keller-pencil-genus-review-grok46-20260902.md:261:2g_L − 2  =  Z·R_aff + n(W−S) − N − κ.
/private/var/folders/80/jm5p82hn56g0crpvv9xjzrc00000gn/T/jc2-lane.9FRnN1/inputs/keller-pencil-genus-review-grok46-20260902.md:264:In family (B), two independent computations give `Z·R_aff = N−1` (fibre: one affine point `w=0` with `ord(w)=m`, contribution `m−1`; branch: `Jac = m x y^{m−1}`, `{y=0}` maps with degree 1 onto a line, `{x=0}` is contracted). The divergent piece is `n(W−S)=k(m−1)`, linear in `k`. Deleting a term bounded by `N` from a quantity that diverges linearly in `k` leaves a quantity that still diverges linearly in `k`. Equivalently, the hypothetical Keller substitution `R_aff=0` *keeping the same* `(n,W,S,κ)` still has `2g−2 = k(m−1)−m−gcd(k−1,m) → ∞`.
/private/var/folders/80/jm5p82hn56g0crpvv9xjzrc00000gn/T/jc2-lane.9FRnN1/inputs/keller-pencil-genus-review-grok46-20260902.md:266:**What “alone” is.** The only use of `Jac F ∈ C^*` in NVM’s intersection ledger is `R_aff=0`, which converts the general pairing into `NOETHER-K` `Z·K_X = −2N −κ + n(W−S)`. That identity does not bound `n(W−S)` or `Psi`. Combined with FORK-GENUS, `n(W−S) = 2N − Lambda + Psi`, so `NOETHER-K` rewrites the ceiling as a bound on fork mass and does not supply one. This is a theorem about this ledger.
/private/var/folders/80/jm5p82hn56g0crpvv9xjzrc00000gn/T/jc2-lane.9FRnN1/inputs/keller-pencil-genus-review-grok46-20260902.md:268:**What “alone” is not.** Keller also forces: étaleness on fibres (UNIT-SPEED, a wash); smoothness of `C_L`; singularity of `A_F` (the residue PROFILE-WITNESS does not match); and whatever constraints étaleness plus `Pic(A^2)=0` impose on the *shape* of `T_+`. The producer’s “only place left in the ledger is the polar tree” (`KPG:538-539,601-604`) is true **inside the NVM pairing ledger**. It is not a theorem that every other Keller consequence is useless. `OPEN[SING-WITNESS]` is exactly the other door, and a `NO` there would localise the ceiling in the singularity requirement rather than in `Psi`.
/private/var/folders/80/jm5p82hn56g0crpvv9xjzrc00000gn/T/jc2-lane.9FRnN1/inputs/keller-pencil-genus-review-grok46-20260902.md:274:## 7. ATYPICAL-LEDGER and the `N=4` control
/private/var/folders/80/jm5p82hn56g0crpvv9xjzrc00000gn/T/jc2-lane.9FRnN1/inputs/keller-pencil-genus-review-grok46-20260902.md:276:`A_F`-bar is dominated by dicriticals `≅ P^1`, hence rational when irreducible. Projection from generic `z_u∈L_∞` is degree `n`; RH gives ramification `2n−2`, of which `n−1` sits at the unique place at infinity, leaving `τ + Σ(mult_P−r_P)=n−1` (`KPG:358-367`). Suzuki `Σ λ_c = nW−N+1` is the same identity. Vanishing cycles: `H_1(A^2)=0` plus `Σ λ_c=b_1(C_gen)` is tight; no inequality (`KPG:375-382`). At `N=4` (B3), `n=4` forces `(g,θ)=(0,2)`, `b_1=5`, `τ=2`, `Σλ=5`. Agrees with `KPG:384-396`.
